(e) if, in consequence of the acquisition of the land, the person interested is compelled to change his residence or place of business, the reasonable expenses, if any, incidental to such change; and (f) the damage, if any, bona fide resulting from diminution of the profits of the land between the time of the publication of the notification under sub-section (1) of section 4 and the time of the publication of the declaration under sub- section (2) of section 9.
Section 14- Method of determining compensation.
From a bare reading of these provisions, it is apparent that where the land is acquired under Section 9, compensation shall be determined taking into consideration the market value, damages sustained by the person and the fact whether the person interested is compelled to change his residence or place of business, the reasonable expenses thereof, the damage resulting from diminution of the profits of the land.
In the present case, the fathers/mother of the petitioners entered into an agreement and the amount of compensation was duly paid in accordance with the terms and conditions of the agreements,
therefore, in the opinion of this Court, no case is made out to interfere with the procedure adopted by the NTPC in award or quantum of compensation.
